entityDescription:
Geocart S.p.A. is an Engineering Company that provides technical services in the following fields: Earth Observation, Environment, Civil Protection, Energy, Information and Communication Technology, Civil Engineering. Geocart offers services and provides products that respond to national and international advanced marketing needs and relevant challenges, designing and carrying out innovative solutions and tools for surveying the territory, monitoring the environment and detecting infrastructures anomalies. The developed activities focus on the design, production and maintenance of geographic databases. The Company provides services of satellite image processing and refining-modeling geographic data coming from terrestrial and aerial mapping, using traditional and innovative techniques and instrumentation (GPS, laser scanner, photogrammetric cameras and sensors operating in different spectral bands), including the planning and development of Geographic Information Systems, cartographic editing and software solutions specifically developed on Customer&rsquo;s requirements. Geocart is certified in conformity with UNI EN ISO 9001:2015 relatively to the following purposes:
&bull; Aerial and ground surveying and data processing services for the characterization, modelling and monitoring of infrastructures, civil works and cultural heritage, territory and environment, aerial inspections of power lines.
&bull; Research and development of integrated services, techniques and algorithms based on ground, aerial and satellite Earth Observations. Design and development of software applications, information systems and GIS.
&bull; Design of High Voltage/Medium Voltage power lines.
Since 2001 Geocart performs on behalf of electricity distribution companies aerial inspection services on high and medium voltage distribution networks through the use of advanced remote sensing techniques. Up to now, more than 500,000 km of networks have been inspected on national and foreign territories. The main international markets are Spain, Romania and Latin America (Brazil and Chile). 
In general, the main services provided by Geocart can be summarized as follows:
&middot; aerial surveys allowing the acquisition of territorial and environmental data, as well as the survey of technological networks or infrastructures, through the use of aircraft/ helicopters/drones and the use of high innovative technologies (modular aerial platforms integrating various kind of sensors including Lidar, digital and thermal cameras, hyperspectral sensors, etc.);
&middot; terrestrial Lidar surveys and processing of the acquired data aimed to a high detailed geometric reconstruction of single structures, buildings or historical monuments;
&middot; processing of raw data acquired from airborne and/or terrestrial surveys with dedicated software aimed to produce high precision DTM/DSM, orthophotos, technical and thematic cartography, environmental studies or technical elaborations;
&middot; processing of satellite data, both optical and radar, for the estimation of surface movements, changes in land use/coverage or for producing thematic maps;
&middot; design and development of geographic and territorial information systems;
&middot; development of software applications customer oriented for the use of spatial or environmental data;
&middot; modeling of technological infrastructures in support of on demand earth observation services;
&middot; virtual reality from remote sensing data through the use of advanced computer graphics techniques.

